# Pairs with EventualConvergence in ReplicationReBootstrap. Reproduces production
# before #4678 (#4615): the reap waited only for the wall-clock grace period, so a
# late write the tombstone beats resurrects the key at s, while r holds the delete.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceReapInsideGrace
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a tombstone is reaped while a write it beats is still on its way, which then resurrects the key
PERTURBS: Reap

--- FIND
    /\ \A o \in Others : \A i \in (cursor[<<o, s>>] + 1)..Len(wal[o]) : wal[o][i].h > reg[s].h
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no grace period.
    /\ TRUE
--- END
